SUMMARY:Constitution Day Program
DESCRIPTION:Join the American Constitution Society\, the Federalist Socie
 ty\, and the Maurer School of Law for a conversation on the scope of pres
 idential authority over war powers\, featuring guest speakers Robert F. T
 urner and Scott R. Anderson.  RSVP below by 4 pm on Friday\, September 11
  to attend.  Food will be provided to those who RSVP.&#160\;_____________
 _________________________________________________Robert F. Turner was a c
 o-founder\, Distinguished Fellow\, and Professor at the University of Vir
 ginia's Center for National Security Law. He was also the Charles H. Stoc
 kton Chair of International Law at the U.S. Naval War College. Professor 
 Turner currently serves as a nonresident senior fellow at George Mason Un
 iversity's National Security Institute.Scott R. Anderson is a Senior Fell
 ow in Governance Studies at the Brookings Institution and General Counsel
  and Senior Editor at Lawfare. He is also a nonresident Senior Fellow wit
 h the National Security Program at Columbia Law School. Previously\, Ande
 rson served as an attorney-adviser for the U.S. Department of State and a
 s the legal adviser for the U.S. Embassy in Baghdad\, Iraq.&#160\;
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Join the American Constitution Society\
 , the Federalist Society\, and the Maurer School of Law for a conversatio
 n on the scope of presidential authority over war powers\, featuring gues
 t speakers Robert F. Turner and Scott R. Anderson.</p><p>  RSVP below by 
 4 pm on Friday\, September 11 to attend.</p><p>  Food will be provided to
  those who RSVP.&#160\;</p><p><strong>___________________________________
 ___________________________</strong></p><p><strong>Robert F. Turner</stro
 ng> was a co-founder\, Distinguished Fellow\, and Professor at the Univer
 sity of Virginia's Center for National Security Law. He was also the Char
 les H. Stockton Chair of International Law at the U.S. Naval War College.
  Professor Turner currently serves as a nonresident senior fellow at Geor
 ge Mason University's National Security Institute.</p><p><strong>Scott R.
  Anderson</strong> is a Senior Fellow in Governance Studies at the Brooki
 ngs Institution and General Counsel and Senior Editor at Lawfare. He is a
 lso a nonresident Senior Fellow with the National Security Program at Col
 umbia Law School. Previously\, Anderson served as an attorney-adviser for
  the U.S. Department of State and as the legal adviser for the U.S. Embas
 sy in Baghdad\, Iraq.&#160\;</p>
