BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU Maurer School of Law
DTSTART:20260923T160000Z
DTEND:20260923T170000Z
LOCATION:Lowell E. Baier Hall - DeLaney Moot Court Room - 123
GEO:39.165074;-86.526424
SUMMARY:Barnes & Thornburg: The Intersections of Science\, Law\, and Oppo
 rtunities in Litigation
DESCRIPTION:Join William E. Padgett\, Partner (Maurer '94)\, and Kathleen
  Waak (Maurer '20)\, Associate\, at Barnes &amp\; Thornburg for a discuss
 ion on "The Intersections of Science\, Law\, and Opportunities in Litigat
 ion."  Padgett and Waak practice in Barnes &amp\; Thornburg's Drug\, Devi
 ce and Consumer Products (DDCP) and Product Liability and Mass Torts (PLM
 T) practice groups. These nationally recognized groups are the largest pr
 actice groups at the 800+ attorney firm. Drawing on their work at Barnes 
 &amp\; Thornburg\, they will share how science and law intersect in their
  litigation practices and introduce students to opportunities in these ar
 eas of practice.  No background in science is necessary. All Maurer stude
 nts are welcome and encouraged to attend.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Join William E. Padgett\, Partner (Maur
 er '94)\, and Kathleen Waak (Maurer '20)\, Associate\, at Barnes &amp\; T
 hornburg for a discussion on "The Intersections of Science\, Law\, and Op
 portunities in Litigation."</p><p>  Padgett and Waak practice in Barnes &
 amp\; Thornburg's Drug\, Device and Consumer Products (DDCP) and Product 
 Liability and Mass Torts (PLMT) practice groups. These nationally recogni
 zed groups are the largest practice groups at the 800+ attorney firm. Dra
 wing on their work at Barnes &amp\; Thornburg\, they will share how scien
 ce and law intersect in their litigation practices and introduce students
  to opportunities in these areas of practice.</p><p>  No background in sc
 ience is necessary. All Maurer students are welcome and encouraged to att
 end.</p>
UID:20260923T160000Z-2401705@events.iu.edu
DTSTAMP:20260830T162123Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/lawiub/event/2401705-cso-program
